1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:04,000
The traditional lasagna in the making from Roccos of Rockaway Beach in Queens.

2
00:00:04,580 --> 00:00:06,940
Lasagna sheets get boiled and it's time to layer.

3
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:16,359
First, their house-made meat ragu, some ricotta cheese, parmesan cheese, mozzarella, fresh basil, and their bechamel.

4
00:00:17,179 --> 00:00:25,219
Another layer of pasta sheets, more meat ragu, ricotta cheese, parmesan, mozzarella, basil, bechamel.

5
00:00:26,039 --> 00:00:29,420
If you've been following us for a while, you know how much we love lasagna,

6
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:35,299
and we've heard some great things about this spot, so needless to say, we were super excited to devour this.

7
00:00:36,039 --> 00:00:40,420
They continue to repeat this process until they build five freaking layers.

8
00:00:43,719 --> 00:00:46,380
The last pasta sheets of the lasagna get tucked in,

9
00:00:47,329 --> 00:00:51,799
and they top it with more meat ragu, a healthy amount of parmesan cheese,

10
00:00:52,619 --> 00:00:53,420
and fresh mozzarella.

11
00:00:54,280 --> 00:00:56,780
Into the cold brick pizza oven until it looks like this.

